","person_slug":"shayne-neumann","vote":"no"},{"name":"Stephen Jones","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10740","person_slug":"stephen-jones","vote":"no"},{"name":"Steve Georganas","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10245","person_slug":"steve-georganas","vote":"no"},{"name":"Stuart Robert","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10545","person_slug":"stuart-robert","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Susan Templeman","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10873","person_slug":"susan-templeman","vote":"no"},{"name":"Sussan Ley","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10387","person_slug":"sussan-ley","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Tanya Plibersek","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10513","person_slug":"tanya-plibersek","vote":"no"},{"name":"Ted O'Brien","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10866","person_slug":"ted-obrien","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Terri Butler","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10825","person_slug":"terri-butler","vote":"no"},{"name":"Terry Young","party":"LNP","person_id":"tvfy_10933","person_slug":"terry-young","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Tim Watts","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10794","person_slug":"tim-watts","vote":"no"},{"name":"Tim Wilson","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10894","person_slug":"tim-wilson","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Tony Burke","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10081","person_slug":"tony-burke","vote":"no"},{"name":"Tony Pasin","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10784","person_slug":"tony-pasin","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Tony Zappia","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10695","person_slug":"tony-zappia","vote":"no"},{"name":"Vince Connelly","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10939","person_slug":"vince-connelly","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Warren Snowdon","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10599","person_slug":"warren-snowdon","vote":"no"},{"name":"Zali Steggall","party":"Independent","person_id":"tvfy_10941","person_slug":"zali-steggall","vote":"aye"}],"name":"Higher Education Legislation Amendment (Provider Category Standards and Other Measures) Bill 2020 - Second Reading - Keep motion unchanged","noes":47,"question":"The majority voted in favour of a [motion](https://www.openaustralia.org.au/debate/?id=2020-11-12.11.2) to keep the original wording of the [second reading motion](https://peo.gov.au/understand-our-parliament/how-parliament-works/bills-and-laws/making-a-law-in-the-australian-parliament/) unchanged. A second reading motion is \"*that the bill be read a second time*,\" which is parliamentary jargon for agreeing with the main idea of the bill. The change was proposed by the MP For Moreton [Graham Perrett](https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/people/representatives/moreton/graham_perrett) (Labor). ### Proposed change > *That all words after \"That\" be omitted with a view to substituting the following words:* > > *\"whilst not declining to give the bill a second reading, the House notes that the Government has:* > > *(1) damaged the quality of Australia's world-class education system;* > > *(2) abandoned university workers during the pandemic;* > > *(3) cut billions in funding and made it harder and more expensive for students to go to university; and* > > *(4) done nothing that will help young people get into priority courses and jobs\".*","result":"affirmative","slug":"division-federal-representatives-6716","source_url":"https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/divisions/representatives/2020-11-12/1"}
